+<!-- [advc.104x] This file used to be called BBAI_AI_Variables_GlobalDefines.xml; now also contains UWAI parameters. -->
+<!-- UWAI breaks down the computation of AI war utility into a sum of 28 "aspects", most of which are either in favor of war (added to the total war utility) or against war (subtracted). There are a few mixed aspects that could either increase or decrease war utility. Each aspect corresponds to one particular motivation for or against war. Through this file, a weight is assigned to each aspect. This weight is interpreted as a percentage by which the aspect utility is multiplied. The default (recommended) weights are all 100. This doesn't imply though that all aspects contribute equally by default; the weights are only a final adjustment to the (hardcoded) formulas.-->
+<!-- A weight of e.g. 50 halves the default impact of an aspect, 200 doubles it. 0 means that the aspect is entirely disregarded. A negative weight (not recommended) turns a pro-war aspect into an anti-war aspect or vice versa. In the descriptions below, "we" refers to the AI civ that is considering war. [advc.104x] -->
+<!-- <Civ4Defines xmlns="x-schema:CIV4GlobalDefinesSchema.xml"> -->
+	<Define>
+		<!-- The cities we expect to conquer as economic assets. -->
+		<DefineName>UWAI_WEIGHT_GREED_FOR_ASSETS</DefineName>
+		<iDefineIntVal>100</iDefineIntVal>
+	</Define>
+	<Define>
+		<!-- The economic value of accepted capitulations. (Not: Getting closer to a Conquest victory; that's handled under MILITARY_VICTORY.) -->
+		<DefineName>UWAI_WEIGHT_GREED_FOR_VASSALS</DefineName>
+		<iDefineIntVal>100</iDefineIntVal>
+	</Define>
+	<Define>
+		<!-- By eliminating a civ early in the game, some of the unsettled land near it can be settled and exploited. Lebensraum if you will (and in Civ, it actually works).  -->
+		<DefineName>UWAI_WEIGHT_GREED_FOR_SPACE</DefineName>
+		<iDefineIntVal>100</iDefineIntVal>
+	</Define>
+	<Define>
+		<!-- Just the value of expected reparations really. Sponsored war is covered by HIRED_HAND. -->
+		<DefineName>UWAI_WEIGHT_GREED_FOR_CASH</DefineName>
+		<iDefineIntVal>100</iDefineIntVal>
+	</Define>
+	<Define>
+		<!-- The satisfaction of seeing our (worst) enemies devastated. -->
+		<!-- custom: seeing worst enemy defeated should not matter as much as seeing ourselves grow maybe, decreasing this a bit so hopefully AI is a bit more effective, was 100 -->
+		<DefineName>UWAI_WEIGHT_LOATHING</DefineName>
+		<iDefineIntVal>70</iDefineIntVal>
+	</Define>
+	<Define>
+		<!-- The prospect of a speedy military victory incites us to wage war. This covers Domination, Conquest and Diplomatic victory; Diplo victory also factors into ILL_WILL. -->
+		<!-- custom: slightly increase war propension if we are likely to win, but not increasing it a lot, as there is a risk too of going too soon to war (exposure to other rivals, risk if war fails, slower economy short term, was 100)-->
+		<DefineName>UWAI_WEIGHT_MILITARY_VICTORY</DefineName>
+		<iDefineIntVal>105</iDefineIntVal>
+	</Define>
+	<Define>
+		<!-- Protect our partners because we want to continue trading with
+			 them, and don't want to become isolated. Assistance for more
+			 principled reasons is covered by FIDELITY, the "mutual struggle"
+			 diplo bonus by SUCKING_UP. -->
+		<!-- custom: as much as we like our partners, it is in our interest if
+		rivals fight each other, we conquer back the cities they lost, liberate
+		it for them to gain favour, or keep it as our expansion, was 100 -->
+		<DefineName>UWAI_WEIGHT_PRESERVATION_OF_PARTNERS</DefineName>
+		<iDefineIntVal>80</iDefineIntVal>
+	</Define>
+  <!-- The next four - Reconquista, Rebuke, Fidelity and Hired Hand - are about
+	   upholding a reputation. Since Civ 4 doesn't have a reputation system,
+	   this is mostly (irrational) role-playing. -->
+	<Define>
+		<!-- By reconquering previously owned cities, we show that it's not
+			 worthwhile to conquer our cities; we'll get them back. -->
+		<!-- custom: city has our culture, so worth more and easier to benefit from
+		than a rival's city. It may sometimes be wise to give up the city short	term
+		or even mid or long term maybe too sometimes so not increasing it a lot,
+		was 100 
+		May be especially more important to defend our cities and their religion
+		now with the future religion changes i made, was 100 -->
+		<DefineName>UWAI_WEIGHT_RECONQUISTA</DefineName>
+		<iDefineIntVal>130</iDefineIntVal>
+	</Define>
+	<Define>
+		<!-- We show we can take by force what was denied to us when we
